{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.10.0"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":true}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 🛡️ Guard Zone Monitoring System — v2 (InsightFace Edition)\n### Integrated with your teammate's face recognition system\n\n---\n## 📋 WHAT CHANGED FROM v1?\n\nYour teammate used **InsightFace** (buffalo_l model) instead of the `face_recognition` library.\nInsightFace is **more accurate** and **faster on GPU**. Here's what was taken from their notebook:\n\n| Their Code | Where It Goes | What It Does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `insightface` + `buffalo_l` model | Phase 1 + Phase 3 | Detects face AND generates 512-number embedding in one call |\n| `get_face_embedding()` | **Phase 1** — Enrollment | Converts guard photo → 512-number face fingerprint |\n| `cosine similarity` math | **Phase 3** — Recognition | Compares faces using `1 - cosine(a, b)` formula |\n| `process_matching_stream()` loop | **Phase 4** — Detection | Frame-by-frame face matching (we ADD zone check + alerts into this) |\n| `process_video_to_folder()` | **Phase 1 helper** | Extracts face crops from video for enrollment |\n\n---\n## ⚠️ BEFORE YOU START:\n1. **Settings → Accelerator → GPU T4** (InsightFace needs GPU)\n2. Upload the guard's reference photo via **Add Data**\n3. Upload your video via **Add Data**\n4. Run cells **one by one** top to bottom\n---","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 📦 CELL 1 — Install Libraries\n\n**Key difference from v1:** We now install `insightface` + `onnxruntime-gpu` instead of `dlib` + `face_recognition`.\nInsightFace uses ONNX models that run directly on the GPU — much faster.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# insightface = your teammate's face detection + recognition library\n# It uses two models inside 'buffalo_l':\n#   - SCRFD: detects WHERE faces are in the frame\n#   - ArcFace: generates a 512-number face fingerprint (embedding)\n!pip install insightface --quiet\n\n# onnxruntime-gpu = the engine that runs InsightFace models on the GPU\n# Without this, InsightFace falls back to CPU (much slower)\n!pip install onnxruntime-gpu --quiet\n\n# scipy = math library — we use it for cosine distance calculation\n# Your teammate used: similarity = 1 - cosine(embedding_A, embedding_B)\n!pip install scipy --quiet\n\n# opencv-python = image and video processing (reading frames, drawing boxes, etc.)\n!pip install opencv-python --quiet\n\nprint(\"✅ All libraries installed!\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 📥 CELL 2 — Import Everything","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import cv2                              # OpenCV — video/image processing\nimport numpy as np                      # math operations on arrays\nimport pickle                           # save/load Python objects to files\nimport os                               # file and folder operations\nimport json                             # save/load data as text\nimport time                             # timestamps\nimport datetime                         # human-readable date/time\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt         # display images in the notebook\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cosine  # cosine distance — from your teammate's code\nfrom insightface.app import FaceAnalysis   # InsightFace — your teammate's library\n\nprint(\"✅ All imports successful!\")\nprint(\"OpenCV version:\", cv2.__version__)","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## ⚙️ CELL 3 — Initialize InsightFace Model\n\nThis is the **core of your teammate's system**. The `buffalo_l` model does two jobs:\n- **Detection**: finds where faces are (bounding boxes)\n- **Recognition**: converts each face into a 512-number fingerprint (embedding)\n\nWe initialize it ONCE here and reuse it everywhere.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# FaceAnalysis loads the InsightFace model pipeline\n# name='buffalo_l' = the 'large' version of the buffalo model\n#   - More accurate than 'buffalo_s' (small), worth it since we have GPU\n# providers list = which hardware to use, in priority order\n#   - 'CUDAExecutionProvider' = GPU (fast)\n#   - 'CPUExecutionProvider'  = CPU fallback (if GPU fails)\n# THIS LINE IS DIRECTLY FROM YOUR TEAMMATE'S NOTEBOOK\napp = FaceAnalysis(\n    name='buffalo_l',\n    providers=['CUDAExecutionProvider', 'CPUExecutionProvider']\n)\n\n# prepare() downloads the model weights (first run only) and sets up GPU\n# ctx_id=0 = use the first GPU (GPU index 0)\n# det_size=(640, 640) = internal resolution for face detection\n#   - Larger = finds smaller faces but slower\n#   - 640x640 is the sweet spot your teammate chose\napp.prepare(ctx_id=0, det_size=(640, 640))\n\nprint(\"✅ InsightFace buffalo_l model loaded and ready!\")\nprint(\"Model handles both: face DETECTION + face RECOGNITION (ArcFace 512-D embeddings)\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n# 🔵 PHASE 1 — GUARD ENROLLMENT\n\n**Your teammate's contribution here:**\n- `get_face_embedding()` function — converts a photo into a 512-number face fingerprint\n- `process_video_to_folder()` function — if you don't have a photo, extract face crops from a video first\n\n**What we ADD:**\n- Save the embedding to a `.pkl` file so the detection loop can load it later\n- Support storing multiple guards\n\n---\n## CELL 4 — `get_face_embedding()` — FROM YOUR TEAMMATE'S CODE","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# THIS FUNCTION IS DIRECTLY FROM YOUR TEAMMATE'S NOTEBOOK\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\ndef get_face_embedding(image_path):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a face photo into a 512-number mathematical fingerprint.\n    \n    How it works:\n    - Load the image\n    - Run InsightFace to detect all faces\n    - Take the first (largest) face found\n    - Return its 'normed_embedding' — a 512-number normalized vector\n      that uniquely describes this person's face\n    \n    Returns: numpy array of 512 numbers, or None if no face found\n    \"\"\"\n    img = cv2.imread(image_path)    # load image from disk\n    if img is None:                  # if path was wrong, imread returns None\n        print(f\"❌ Could not load image: {image_path}\")\n        return None\n    \n    faces = app.get(img)             # run InsightFace — detects faces AND generates embeddings\n    if not faces:                    # if no faces were detected in this image\n        print(\"❌ No face detected in image!\")\n        return None\n    \n    # faces is a list of detected faces, sorted by confidence\n    # faces[0] = first/best face\n    # .normed_embedding = the 512-number vector, already normalized (length = 1.0)\n    # Normalization means cosine similarity works cleanly\n    return faces[0].normed_embedding\n\n\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# THIS FUNCTION IS ALSO FROM YOUR TEAMMATE'S NOTEBOOK\n# Use this if you don't have a clear photo — extract faces from a video first\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\ndef extract_faces_from_video(video_path, output_dir='extracted_faces', max_frames=300):\n    \"\"\"\n    Scans a video and saves cropped face images to a folder.\n    Use this to get a clean reference photo of the guard if you only have a video.\n    \n    Parameters:\n        video_path : path to the video file\n        output_dir : folder name to save face crops\n        max_frames : stop after this many frames (saves time)\n    \"\"\"\n    faces_path = os.path.join(\"/kaggle/working/\", output_dir)\n    os.makedirs(faces_path, exist_ok=True)   # create folder if it doesn't exist\n\n    # Detection-only app (faster — we don't need embeddings here, just crops)\n    det_app = FaceAnalysis(\n        allowed_modules=['detection'],        # only load the detection model, skip ArcFace\n        providers=['CUDAExecutionProvider', 'CPUExecutionProvider']\n    )\n    det_app.prepare(ctx_id=0, det_size=(640, 640))\n\n    cap = cv2.VideoCapture(video_path)        # open the video file\n    if not cap.isOpened():\n        print(f\"❌ Cannot open video: {video_path}\")\n        return\n\n    frame_count = 0\n    faces_saved = 0\n    padding = 0.45   # how much extra space to add around the face (45%)\n    # Your teammate chose 0.45 to include the full head, not just the face\n\n    print(f\"🚀 Extracting face crops from video (max {max_frames} frames)...\")\n\n    while cap.isOpened():\n        ret, frame = cap.read()              # read next frame\n        if not ret or frame_count >= max_frames:\n            break\n\n        frame_count += 1\n        h_img, w_img, _ = frame.shape       # get frame dimensions\n        faces = det_app.get(frame)          # detect faces\n\n        for i, face in enumerate(faces):\n            if face.det_score < 0.6:        # skip low-confidence detections\n                continue                    # det_score 0.6 = your teammate's threshold\n\n            bbox = face.bbox.astype(int)    # face bounding box as integers\n            x1, y1, x2, y2 = bbox[0], bbox[1], bbox[2], bbox[3]\n            w, h = x2 - x1, y2 - y1        # face width and height\n\n            # Add padding around the face crop (your teammate's logic)\n            # 1.8x vertical padding on top = captures forehead + hair\n            x_start = int(max(0, x1 - (w * padding)))\n            y_start = int(max(0, y1 - (h * padding * 1.8)))\n            x_end   = int(min(w_img, x2 + (w * padding)))\n            y_end   = int(min(h_img, y2 + (h * padding)))\n\n            head_roi = frame[y_start:y_end, x_start:x_end]  # crop the head region\n\n            if head_roi.size > 0:           # only save if crop is not empty\n                filename = os.path.join(faces_path, f\"face_{frame_count:04d}_{i}.jpg\")\n                cv2.imwrite(filename, head_roi)\n                faces_saved += 1\n\n        if frame_count % 50 == 0:\n            print(f\"  Frame {frame_count} | Faces saved: {faces_saved}\")\n\n    cap.release()\n    print(f\"\\n✅ Done! {faces_saved} face crops saved to: {faces_path}\")\n    print(\"Browse the Output sidebar → pick the clearest face image as your reference photo.\")\n\n\nprint(\"✅ get_face_embedding() and extract_faces_from_video() are ready!\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## CELL 5 — Enroll the Guard (Save Embedding)\n\n**Flow:** Load guard photo → `get_face_embedding()` (teammate's function) → save to `.pkl` file","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPTION A: You already have a clear photo of the guard\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ← CHANGE THIS to your uploaded guard photo path\nGUARD_PHOTO_PATH = \"/kaggle/input/your-dataset/guard.jpg\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPTION B: You only have a video — uncomment and run this block first\n# Then look at the extracted faces in the Output sidebar,\n# pick the best one, and use that path as GUARD_PHOTO_PATH above\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# VIDEO_FOR_ENROLLMENT = \"/kaggle/input/your-dataset/your_video.mp4\"\n# extract_faces_from_video(VIDEO_FOR_ENROLLMENT, max_frames=150)\n# # Then set: GUARD_PHOTO_PATH = \"/kaggle/working/extracted_faces/face_0010_0.jpg\"\n\n# Type the guard's name when prompted\nGUARD_NAME = input(\"Enter the guard's name: \").strip()\nif GUARD_NAME == \"\":\n    GUARD_NAME = \"Guard_01\"\n    print(\"No name entered. Using: Guard_01\")\n\n# ── GENERATE EMBEDDING USING TEAMMATE'S FUNCTION ──\nprint(f\"\\nGenerating face embedding for: {GUARD_NAME}\")\nprint(\"Using InsightFace ArcFace model (your teammate's system)...\")\n\nguard_embedding = get_face_embedding(GUARD_PHOTO_PATH)\n# This calls your teammate's get_face_embedding() from Cell 4\n# Returns a numpy array of 512 numbers\n\nif guard_embedding is None:\n    print(\"❌ Enrollment failed. Fix the image path or use a clearer photo.\")\nelse:\n    print(f\"✅ Embedding generated!\")\n    print(f\"   Embedding size: {len(guard_embedding)} numbers (ArcFace 512-D vector)\")\n    print(f\"   First 5 values: {guard_embedding[:5].round(4)}\")\n\n    # ── SHOW THE GUARD PHOTO WITH DETECTED FACE BOX ──\n    img_show = cv2.imread(GUARD_PHOTO_PATH)\n    faces_in_photo = app.get(img_show)\n    if faces_in_photo:\n        bbox = faces_in_photo[0].bbox.astype(int)\n        cv2.rectangle(img_show, (bbox[0], bbox[1]), (bbox[2], bbox[3]), (0, 255, 0), 3)\n        cv2.putText(img_show, f\"{GUARD_NAME} — Enrolled\",\n                    (bbox[0], bbox[1]-10), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.8, (0,255,0), 2)\n\n    plt.figure(figsize=(6,6))\n    plt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(img_show, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n    plt.title(f\"Guard Photo: {GUARD_NAME}\")\n    plt.axis('off')\n    plt.show()\n\n    # ── SAVE EMBEDDING TO FILE ──\n    DATA_FOLDER = \"/kaggle/working/guard_data\"\n    os.makedirs(DATA_FOLDER, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Dictionary: guard name → 512-number embedding\n    # Using a dict allows adding more guards later\n    guard_database = {GUARD_NAME: guard_embedding}\n\n    ENCODING_FILE = os.path.join(DATA_FOLDER, \"guard_encodings.pkl\")\n    with open(ENCODING_FILE, \"wb\") as f:   # \"wb\" = write binary\n        pickle.dump(guard_database, f)      # pickle converts dict → binary bytes\n\n    print(f\"\\n✅ Saved to: {ENCODING_FILE}\")\n\n    # Verify the save worked by loading it back\n    with open(ENCODING_FILE, \"rb\") as f:\n        check = pickle.load(f)\n    print(f\"Verified — Guards enrolled: {list(check.keys())}\")\n    print(\"\\n✅ PHASE 1 COMPLETE — Guard enrolled with InsightFace ArcFace embedding!\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n# 🟡 PHASE 2 — ZONE DEFINITION\n\nThis phase is **100% new** — your teammate's notebook had no zone concept.\nWe define the polygon area where the guard must stay.\n\n---\n## CELL 6 — Define the Allowed Zone","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ── VIDEO FRAME SIZE ──\n# Set to match your video's resolution\n# Common sizes: 640x480, 1280x720, 1920x1080\nFRAME_WIDTH  = 640\nFRAME_HEIGHT = 480\n\n# ── HOW COORDINATES WORK ──\n# (0,0) = TOP-LEFT corner of the frame\n# x goes RIGHT →,  y goes DOWN ↓\n# Example for 640x480: bottom-right corner = (640, 480)\n\n# ── DEFINE ZONE CORNERS ──\n# Change these (x, y) coordinates to match the actual guard post location\n# This example: a rectangle in the center of the frame\nzone_points = np.array([\n    [160, 120],   # top-left corner of zone\n    [480, 120],   # top-right corner of zone\n    [480, 360],   # bottom-right corner of zone\n    [160, 360],   # bottom-left corner of zone\n], dtype=np.int32)\n# dtype=np.int32 is REQUIRED by OpenCV polygon drawing functions\n\nprint(\"Zone corners:\")\nfor i, pt in enumerate(zone_points):\n    print(f\"  Corner {i+1}: x={pt[0]}, y={pt[1]}\")\n\n# ── VISUALIZE THE ZONE ──\nblank = np.zeros((FRAME_HEIGHT, FRAME_WIDTH, 3), dtype=np.uint8)  # black canvas\noverlay = blank.copy()\ncv2.fillPoly(overlay, [zone_points], (0, 80, 0))         # dark green fill\ncv2.polylines(blank, [zone_points], True, (0, 255, 0), 2) # bright green border\nviz = cv2.addWeighted(blank, 0.6, overlay, 0.4, 0)       # blend = semi-transparent fill\n\n# Label the zone center\nzx = int(np.mean(zone_points[:, 0]))   # average of all x values\nzy = int(np.mean(zone_points[:, 1]))   # average of all y values\ncv2.putText(viz, \"ALLOWED ZONE\", (zx-80, zy), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.8, (0,255,0), 2)\ncv2.putText(viz, f\"Frame: {FRAME_WIDTH}x{FRAME_HEIGHT}\", (10, 25),\n            cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.5, (200,200,200), 1)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8,6))\nplt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(viz, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\nplt.title(\"Zone Preview — Guard must stay inside the GREEN area\")\nplt.axis('off')\nplt.show()\nprint(\"✅ Zone defined! Adjust the coordinates above if needed.\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## CELL 7 — Save Zone to File","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"ZONE_FILE = os.path.join(DATA_FOLDER, \"zone_coords.json\")\n\nzone_data = {\n    \"zone_points\": zone_points.tolist(),  # .tolist() converts numpy → plain list (JSON-safe)\n    \"frame_width\": FRAME_WIDTH,\n    \"frame_height\": FRAME_HEIGHT\n}\n\nwith open(ZONE_FILE, \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(zone_data, f, indent=4)     # indent=4 makes the file human-readable\n\nprint(f\"✅ Zone saved to: {ZONE_FILE}\")\n\nwith open(ZONE_FILE, \"r\") as f:\n    print(f.read())\n\nprint(\"✅ PHASE 2 COMPLETE — Zone defined and saved!\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n# 🟢 PHASE 3 — DETECTION HELPERS\n\n**Key change from v1:** The `recognize_face()` function now uses **cosine similarity** (your teammate's method) instead of Euclidean distance.\n\nYour teammate's formula: `similarity = 1 - cosine(embedding_A, embedding_B)`\n- Result near `1.0` = same person\n- Result near `0.0` = different person  \n- Threshold `0.55` = match if similarity > 0.55\n\n---\n## CELL 8 — Load Saved Data","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Load guard face database (saved in Phase 1)\nwith open(ENCODING_FILE, \"rb\") as f:\n    guard_database = pickle.load(f)   # load binary pickle → Python dictionary\n\nknown_names     = list(guard_database.keys())    # [\"Guard_01\", ...]\nknown_embeddings = list(guard_database.values()) # [array([512 numbers]), ...]\n# These are the ArcFace 512-D vectors from your teammate's system\n\nprint(f\"Loaded {len(known_names)} guard(s):\")\nfor name in known_names:\n    print(f\"  - {name}\")\n\n# Load zone coordinates (saved in Phase 2)\nwith open(ZONE_FILE, \"r\") as f:\n    zone_data = json.load(f)\n\nzone_pts = np.array(zone_data[\"zone_points\"], dtype=np.int32)\n# Convert back to numpy array — cv2 polygon functions need numpy dtype=int32\nFRAME_W = zone_data[\"frame_width\"]\nFRAME_H = zone_data[\"frame_height\"]\n\nprint(f\"\\nLoaded zone: {len(zone_pts)} corner points, frame {FRAME_W}x{FRAME_H}\")\nprint(\"✅ All data loaded!\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## CELL 9 — Helper Functions (with teammate's recognition logic)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ── SIMILARITY THRESHOLD ──\n# From your teammate's notebook: threshold=0.55\n# sim > 0.55 = same person (MATCH)\n# sim < 0.55 = different person (Unknown)\n# You can adjust: higher = stricter (fewer false matches), lower = more lenient\nSIMILARITY_THRESHOLD = 0.55\n\n\ndef recognize_face_insightface(face_embedding, known_embeddings, known_names, threshold=SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD):\n    \"\"\"\n    YOUR TEAMMATE'S RECOGNITION LOGIC — adapted for multiple guards.\n    \n    Compares a detected face's embedding against all enrolled guards.\n    Uses cosine similarity: similarity = 1 - cosine(embedding_A, embedding_B)\n    \n    Parameters:\n        face_embedding   : 512-number array from InsightFace for the detected face\n        known_embeddings : list of 512-number arrays for all enrolled guards\n        known_names      : list of guard names matching each embedding\n        threshold        : min similarity to consider a match (default 0.55)\n    \n    Returns:\n        (name, similarity) : name of matched guard + similarity score\n                             name = 'Unknown' if no match above threshold\n    \"\"\"\n    best_name = \"Unknown\"\n    best_sim  = 0.0\n\n    for name, known_emb in zip(known_names, known_embeddings):\n        # zip() pairs each name with its corresponding embedding\n        \n        # YOUR TEAMMATE'S FORMULA: sim = 1 - cosine(A, B)\n        # cosine() returns the distance (0=identical, 1=opposite)\n        # So 1 - distance = similarity (1=identical, 0=opposite)\n        sim = 1 - cosine(known_emb, face_embedding)\n        \n        # Keep track of the best (highest similarity) match\n        if sim > best_sim:\n            best_sim  = sim\n            best_name = name\n\n    # Only return the match if it passed the threshold\n    if best_sim >= threshold:\n        return best_name, best_sim\n    return \"Unknown\", best_sim   # didn't pass threshold — not the enrolled guard\n\n\ndef is_inside_zone(point, polygon):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if a point (x, y) is inside the zone polygon.\n    Uses OpenCV's pointPolygonTest.\n    Returns True if inside or on boundary, False if outside.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = cv2.pointPolygonTest(polygon, (float(point[0]), float(point[1])), False)\n    # float() required — cv2 needs floating point coordinates\n    # False = just check inside/outside, don't compute exact distance\n    # Returns: positive=inside, 0=on boundary, negative=outside\n    return result >= 0\n\n\ndef get_face_center(bbox):\n    \"\"\"\n    Get the center (x, y) of a face bounding box.\n    InsightFace returns bbox as [x1, y1, x2, y2] (different from face_recognition!)\n    \"\"\"\n    x1, y1, x2, y2 = bbox\n    cx = int((x1 + x2) / 2)   # horizontal center\n    cy = int((y1 + y2) / 2)   # vertical center\n    return (cx, cy)\n\n\ndef draw_zone_and_status(frame, zone_polygon, guard_detected, guard_inside_zone, guard_name=\"\"):\n    \"\"\"\n    Draw the monitoring zone on the frame with color-coded status.\n    \n    Color logic:\n      Green  = guard detected AND inside zone → SAFE\n      Red    = guard detected BUT outside zone → ALERT\n      Yellow = guard not detected at all → SEARCHING\n    \"\"\"\n    if guard_detected and guard_inside_zone:\n        color = (0, 255, 0)        # BGR: Green\n        status = f\"SAFE — {guard_name} IN ZONE\"\n    elif guard_detected and not guard_inside_zone:\n        color = (0, 0, 255)        # BGR: Red\n        status = f\"!! ALERT: {guard_name} LEFT ZONE !!\"\n    else:\n        color = (0, 220, 255)      # BGR: Yellow\n        status = \"SEARCHING FOR GUARD...\"\n\n    # Semi-transparent zone fill\n    overlay = frame.copy()\n    cv2.fillPoly(overlay, [zone_polygon], color)\n    cv2.addWeighted(frame, 0.82, overlay, 0.18, 0, frame)\n\n    # Zone border\n    cv2.polylines(frame, [zone_polygon], True, color, 2)\n\n    # Zone label at center\n    zx = int(np.mean(zone_polygon[:, 0]))\n    zy = int(np.mean(zone_polygon[:, 1]))\n    cv2.putText(frame, \"MONITORING ZONE\", (zx-90, zy),\n                cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.5, color, 1)\n\n    # Status bar at top\n    cv2.rectangle(frame, (0, 0), (FRAME_W, 42), (0,0,0), -1)  # black bg\n    cv2.putText(frame, status, (10, 29),\n                cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.68, color, 2)\n\n    return frame\n\n\nprint(\"✅ Helper functions ready!\")\nprint(f\"Recognition: InsightFace ArcFace cosine similarity (threshold={SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD})\")\nprint(\"Functions: recognize_face_insightface(), is_inside_zone(), get_face_center(), draw_zone_and_status()\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## CELL 10 — Alert System","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"ALERT_LOG_FILE = os.path.join(DATA_FOLDER, \"alert_log.txt\")\n\n# Cooldown: min seconds between alerts (prevents log spam)\nALERT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS = 5\nlast_alert_time = 0\n\n\ndef trigger_alert(guard_name, reason, similarity=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Log and print an alert when the guard leaves the zone or disappears.\n    Respects cooldown to avoid hundreds of alerts per second.\n    \"\"\"\n    global last_alert_time\n\n    now = time.time()\n    if now - last_alert_time < ALERT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS:\n        return   # cooldown active — skip this alert\n    last_alert_time = now\n\n    ts = datetime.datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\n    \n    # Include similarity score if provided (helps with tuning the threshold)\n    sim_info = f\" | Similarity: {similarity:.3f}\" if similarity is not None else \"\"\n    msg = f\"[{ts}] ALERT — Guard: {guard_name} | {reason}{sim_info}\"\n\n    print(f\"🚨 {msg}\")\n    \n    with open(ALERT_LOG_FILE, \"a\") as f:\n        f.write(msg + \"\\n\")   # append to log file, \\n = new line\n\n\ndef check_and_alert(guard_detected, guard_in_zone, guard_name, similarity=None):\n    \"\"\"Evaluate current status and trigger alert if guard is missing or outside zone.\"\"\"\n    if not guard_detected:\n        trigger_alert(guard_name, \"Guard NOT detected in frame\")\n    elif not guard_in_zone:\n        trigger_alert(guard_name, \"Guard OUTSIDE allowed zone\", similarity)\n\n\nprint(\"✅ Alert system ready!\")\nprint(f\"Log file: {ALERT_LOG_FILE}\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n# 🔴 PHASE 4 — MAIN DETECTION LOOP\n\n**This is where everything comes together.**  \nYour teammate's `process_matching_stream()` loop is the foundation — we surgically inject the **zone check** and **alert system** right after each face match.\n\n```\nTheir code:            Our additions:\n──────────────────     ───────────────────────────────\napp.get(frame)    →    detect faces (InsightFace)\ncosine similarity →    recognize guard\n                  →  + is_inside_zone()     ← NEW\n                  →  + check_and_alert()    ← NEW  \n                  →  + draw_zone_and_status() ← NEW\nout.write(frame)  →    save output video\n```\n\n---\n## CELL 11A — Test on a Single Image","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ════════════════════════════════════\n# OPTION A: TEST ON A SINGLE IMAGE\n# Quick sanity check — run this first before processing a full video\n# ════════════════════════════════════\n\n# Path to a test image (can be the same enrollment photo for a quick test)\nTEST_IMAGE_PATH = GUARD_PHOTO_PATH   # ← change to a different test image if you have one\n\n# Load and resize image to our frame size\ntest_frame = cv2.imread(TEST_IMAGE_PATH)\ntest_frame = cv2.resize(test_frame, (FRAME_W, FRAME_H))\n\nprint(\"Running InsightFace detection + recognition on test image...\")\n\n# ── DETECT ALL FACES USING INSIGHTFACE ──\n# app.get() is from your teammate's code\n# It returns a list of face objects — each has .bbox, .det_score, .normed_embedding\ndetected_faces = app.get(test_frame)\nprint(f\"Faces detected: {len(detected_faces)}\")\n\n# Tracking variables\nguard_detected   = False\nguard_in_zone    = False\nbest_sim_score   = 0.0\nmatched_name     = known_names[0] if known_names else \"Guard\"\n\n# ── PROCESS EACH DETECTED FACE ──\nfor face in detected_faces:\n\n    # face.normed_embedding = the 512-D ArcFace vector (your teammate's output)\n    name, sim = recognize_face_insightface(\n        face.normed_embedding, known_embeddings, known_names\n    )\n    print(f\"  Face → Name: {name} | Similarity: {sim:.3f}\")\n\n    # face.bbox = [x1, y1, x2, y2] bounding box (InsightFace format)\n    bbox = face.bbox.astype(int)\n\n    if name in known_names:   # ← this is our enrolled guard\n        guard_detected = True\n        matched_name   = name\n        best_sim_score = sim\n\n        # Get face center point to check against zone\n        face_center  = get_face_center(bbox)\n        guard_in_zone = is_inside_zone(face_center, zone_pts)\n\n        print(f\"  Face center: {face_center} | In zone: {guard_in_zone}\")\n\n        # Draw bounding box (green=inside zone, red=outside)\n        box_color = (0, 255, 0) if guard_in_zone else (0, 0, 255)\n        cv2.rectangle(test_frame, (bbox[0], bbox[1]), (bbox[2], bbox[3]), box_color, 2)\n\n        # Label: guard name + similarity score (your teammate showed sim score too)\n        label = f\"{name}: {sim:.2f}\"\n        cv2.putText(test_frame, label, (bbox[0], bbox[1]-10),\n                    cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.7, box_color, 2)\n\n        # Dot at face center\n        cv2.circle(test_frame, face_center, 6, (255, 255, 0), -1)\n\n    else:   # unknown face (not the enrolled guard)\n        cv2.rectangle(test_frame, (bbox[0], bbox[1]), (bbox[2], bbox[3]), (128,128,128), 1)\n        cv2.putText(test_frame, f\"Unknown: {sim:.2f}\", (bbox[0], bbox[1]-10),\n                    cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.6, (128,128,128), 1)\n\n# ── DRAW ZONE ──\ntest_frame = draw_zone_and_status(test_frame, zone_pts, guard_detected, guard_in_zone, matched_name)\n\n# ── ALERT CHECK ──\ncheck_and_alert(guard_detected, guard_in_zone, matched_name, best_sim_score)\n\n# ── SHOW RESULT ──\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\nplt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(test_frame, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\nplt.title(f\"Test Result — {matched_name} | Similarity: {best_sim_score:.3f} | In Zone: {guard_in_zone}\")\nplt.axis('off')\nplt.show()\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*55)\nprint(\"SINGLE IMAGE TEST RESULT:\")\nprint(f\"  Guard detected   : {guard_detected}\")\nprint(f\"  Recognized as    : {matched_name}\")\nprint(f\"  Similarity score : {best_sim_score:.4f} (threshold: {SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD})\")\nprint(f\"  Inside zone      : {guard_in_zone}\")\nprint(f\"  Status           : {'✅ SAFE' if guard_detected and guard_in_zone else '🚨 ALERT'}\")\nprint(\"=\"*55)","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## CELL 11B — Process Full Video (Teammate's Loop + Zone + Alerts)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# OPTION B: PROCESS A FULL VIDEO FILE\n# This is your teammate's process_matching_stream() loop\n# with zone checking and alerts injected into it\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n# ← CHANGE THESE\nVIDEO_INPUT_PATH  = \"/kaggle/input/your-dataset/guard_video.mp4\"\nVIDEO_OUTPUT_PATH = \"/kaggle/working/guard_data/output_monitored.mp4\"\n\n# Process every N frames (your teammate processed every frame, but that's slow)\n# InsightFace is heavier than dlib, so every 2-3 frames is a good balance\nPROCESS_EVERY_N_FRAMES = 2\n\n# ── OPEN VIDEO ──\ncap = cv2.VideoCapture(VIDEO_INPUT_PATH)\nif not cap.isOpened():\n    print(f\"❌ Cannot open video: {VIDEO_INPUT_PATH}\")\nelse:\n    # Read video properties (same as your teammate's code)\n    fps          = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FPS))\n    total_frames = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_COUNT))\n    vid_w        = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_WIDTH))\n    vid_h        = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_HEIGHT))\n\n    print(f\"Input  video: {vid_w}x{vid_h} @ {fps}fps | {total_frames} frames ({total_frames/fps:.1f}s)\")\n\n    # ── SET UP OUTPUT VIDEO WRITER (from your teammate's code) ──\n    fourcc = cv2.VideoWriter_fourcc(*'mp4v')  # MPEG-4 codec for .mp4\n    out = cv2.VideoWriter(VIDEO_OUTPUT_PATH, fourcc, fps, (FRAME_W, FRAME_H))\n\n    # State variables (persist between frames — reuse last known detection)\n    frame_count    = 0\n    guard_detected = False\n    guard_in_zone  = False\n    matched_name   = known_names[0] if known_names else \"Guard\"\n    last_sim       = 0.0\n    total_matches  = 0   # your teammate tracked matches_found\n\n    print(f\"\\n🚀 Scanning video against reference... (InsightFace ArcFace + Zone Check)\")\n    print(f\"Processing every {PROCESS_EVERY_N_FRAMES} frames for speed.\")\n\n    # ── MAIN LOOP — YOUR TEAMMATE'S STRUCTURE + OUR ADDITIONS ──\n    while cap.isOpened():\n        ret, frame = cap.read()     # read next frame from video\n        if not ret:                  # False = end of video\n            print(\"\\n✅ End of video reached\")\n            break\n\n        frame_count += 1\n\n        # Resize to our defined frame size\n        frame = cv2.resize(frame, (FRAME_W, FRAME_H))\n\n        # ── FACE DETECTION + RECOGNITION (every N frames) ──\n        if frame_count % PROCESS_EVERY_N_FRAMES == 0:\n\n            # YOUR TEAMMATE'S LINE: app.get(frame)\n            # Runs both SCRFD (detection) and ArcFace (embedding) in one call\n            faces = app.get(frame)\n\n            # Reset detection state for this pass\n            guard_detected = False\n            guard_in_zone  = False\n\n            for face in faces:\n\n                # YOUR TEAMMATE'S SIMILARITY CALCULATION:\n                # sim = 1 - cosine(target_embedding, face.normed_embedding)\n                name, sim = recognize_face_insightface(\n                    face.normed_embedding, known_embeddings, known_names\n                )\n\n                bbox = face.bbox.astype(int)   # [x1, y1, x2, y2]\n\n                if name in known_names:   # guard recognized!\n                    guard_detected = True\n                    matched_name   = name\n                    last_sim       = sim\n                    total_matches += 1\n\n                    # ── ZONE CHECK ← OUR ADDITION ──\n                    face_center   = get_face_center(bbox)\n                    guard_in_zone = is_inside_zone(face_center, zone_pts)\n\n                    # Draw box (YOUR TEAMMATE'S STYLE: green=match, red=no match)\n                    color = (0, 255, 0) if guard_in_zone else (0, 0, 255)\n                    label = f\"MATCH: {sim:.2f}\"  # keeping teammate's label format\n                    cv2.rectangle(frame, (bbox[0], bbox[1]), (bbox[2], bbox[3]), color, 3)\n                    cv2.putText(frame, label, (bbox[0], bbox[1]-10),\n                                cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.7, color, 2)\n                    cv2.circle(frame, face_center, 5, (255,255,0), -1)\n\n                else:   # unknown face (your teammate's Unknown label)\n                    cv2.rectangle(frame, (bbox[0], bbox[1]), (bbox[2], bbox[3]), (0,0,255), 2)\n                    cv2.putText(frame, f\"Unknown: {sim:.2f}\", (bbox[0], bbox[1]-10),\n                                cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.7, (0,0,255), 2)\n\n            # ── ALERT CHECK ← OUR ADDITION ──\n            check_and_alert(guard_detected, guard_in_zone, matched_name, last_sim)\n\n        # ── DRAW ZONE ON EVERY FRAME ← OUR ADDITION ──\n        frame = draw_zone_and_status(frame, zone_pts, guard_detected, guard_in_zone, matched_name)\n\n        # Frame counter\n        cv2.putText(frame, f\"Frame {frame_count}/{total_frames}\",\n                    (FRAME_W-195, FRAME_H-10), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.45, (180,180,180), 1)\n\n        # ── WRITE FRAME TO OUTPUT VIDEO (your teammate's line) ──\n        out.write(frame)\n\n        # Progress update every 50 frames (your teammate printed every 50)\n        if frame_count % 50 == 0:\n            pct = (frame_count / total_frames) * 100\n            print(f\"  Processed {frame_count} frames... Matches so far: {total_matches} ({pct:.1f}%)\")\n\n    # ── RELEASE RESOURCES (your teammate's cleanup) ──\n    cap.release()   # close input video\n    out.release()   # flush and save output video\n\n    print(f\"\\n✅ Saved processed video: {VIDEO_OUTPUT_PATH}\")\n    print(f\"Total frames: {frame_count} | Total guard matches: {total_matches}\")\n    print(\"Download from the Output panel on the right side of Kaggle.\")\n\n    # ── PREVIEW FIRST FRAME (your teammate did this too) ──\n    preview_cap = cv2.VideoCapture(VIDEO_OUTPUT_PATH)\n    ok, preview = preview_cap.read()\n    if ok:\n        plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n        plt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(preview, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n        plt.title(\"Output Video — First Frame Preview\")\n        plt.axis('off')\n        plt.show()\n    preview_cap.release()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## CELL 12 — Alert Log + Final Report","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"=\" * 62)\nprint(\"          GUARD ZONE MONITORING — FINAL REPORT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 62)\n\n# Alert log summary\nif os.path.exists(ALERT_LOG_FILE):\n    with open(ALERT_LOG_FILE, \"r\") as f:\n        alerts = f.readlines()\n    if len(alerts) == 0:\n        print(\"✅ No alerts. Guard stayed in the zone the entire time.\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Total alerts triggered: {len(alerts)}\\n\")\n        for i, alert in enumerate(alerts, 1):\n            print(f\"{i:3}. {alert.strip()}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No alert log found. Run Cell 11A or 11B first.\")\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"-\" * 62)\nprint(\"SYSTEM CONFIGURATION:\")\nprint(f\"  Face model       : InsightFace buffalo_l (ArcFace 512-D)\")\nprint(f\"  Similarity method: Cosine similarity (your teammate's formula)\")\nprint(f\"  Match threshold  : {SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD} (sim > {SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD} = same person)\")\nprint(f\"  Zone corners     : {len(zone_pts)} points\")\nprint(f\"  Frame size       : {FRAME_W} x {FRAME_H}\")\nprint(\"\\nSAVED FILES:\")\nprint(f\"  Guard embeddings : {ENCODING_FILE}\")\nprint(f\"  Zone coordinates : {ZONE_FILE}\")\nprint(f\"  Alert log        : {ALERT_LOG_FILE}\")\nprint(\"=\" * 62)\nprint(\"\\n✅ ALL 4 PHASES COMPLETE!\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 🗺️ WHAT CAME FROM WHERE\n\n| Code | Source | Phase |\n|---|---|---|\n| `insightface`, `FaceAnalysis(buffalo_l)` | Teammate's notebook | Setup |\n| `app.prepare(ctx_id=0, det_size=(640,640))` | Teammate's notebook | Setup |\n| `get_face_embedding()` | **Teammate's function** | Phase 1 |\n| `extract_faces_from_video()` | **Teammate's function** | Phase 1 helper |\n| Save embedding to `.pkl` | Our addition | Phase 1 |\n| Zone polygon definition | Our addition | Phase 2 |\n| Save zone to `.json` | Our addition | Phase 2 |\n| `recognize_face_insightface()` with `1 - cosine()` | **Teammate's formula** | Phase 3 |\n| `is_inside_zone()` with `pointPolygonTest` | Our addition | Phase 3 |\n| `draw_zone_and_status()` | Our addition | Phase 3 |\n| `app.get(frame)` per-frame loop | **Teammate's loop** | Phase 4 |\n| `sim > threshold` check | **Teammate's logic** | Phase 4 |\n| Zone check + alert injection | Our addition | Phase 4 |\n| Output video writer | Teammate's notebook | Phase 4 |\n\n---\n## 🛠️ TROUBLESHOOTING\n\n| Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `onnxruntime-gpu` install fails | Run `!pip install onnxruntime` (CPU version) as fallback |\n| Guard not recognized | Lower `SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD` from `0.55` to `0.45` |\n| Too many false matches | Raise `SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD` from `0.55` to `0.65` |\n| Video processing very slow | Increase `PROCESS_EVERY_N_FRAMES` to `4` or `5` |\n| Zone in wrong position | Change coordinates in Cell 6, re-run Cells 6 → 7 → 8 |\n| `cv2.imread` returns None | Wrong path. Right-click file in Data panel → Copy path |","metadata":{}}]}